Subject: [PATCH] msm_vidc: keep the Venus firmware loaded

As ../kernel/patches/0020 for 3.10: the video core's firmware was unloaded 15 s
after the last session and loaded again at the next, into a CMA region it needs
whole. After a while in use pages in the region can no longer be moved out, and
from then on every hardware codec fails, the camera's video encoder among them.
Loaded once and never unloaded, it never has to be placed again; an idle core is
power-collapsed either way. The delay stays in debugfs as before.
---
--- drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc_3x/msm_vidc_debug.c
+++ drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc_3x/msm_vidc_debug.c
@@ -27,7 +27,11 @@
 bool msm_vidc_dec_dcvs_mode = true;
 bool msm_vidc_enc_dcvs_mode = true;
 bool msm_vidc_sys_idle_indicator = true;
-int msm_vidc_firmware_unload_delay = 15000;
+/*
+ * Never unload the firmware: loading it again needs venus_mem whole, which after a
+ * while in use the kernel can no longer free.
+ */
+int msm_vidc_firmware_unload_delay = INT_MAX;
 bool msm_vidc_thermal_mitigation_disabled = true;
 bool msm_vidc_bitrate_clock_scaling = 1;
 bool msm_vidc_debug_timeout = true;
